::BEGIN:MAIN
# {{profile.name}} Tutorial

img: {{profile.image}}

## Introduction

p: Welcome to the {{profile.name}} tutorial. {{profile.subtitle}} {{profile.describe}}

p: This tutorial is for the Vectors and for every new entity that joins Deva.world. It teaches one standard way to use the features of {{profile.vector}}: memory, knowledge, search, history, indexes and insert. When every entity calls these features the same way, with the same params and the same limits, then what one entity saves another entity can find, and what one entity finds another entity can check.

p: The tutorial has two kinds of lessons. The feature lessons (Memory through Limits) describe what the code in this version of {{profile.vector}} does today. The convention lessons (Knowledge Cards, Hash Test and Open Items) describe the shared knowledge-card design the Vectors agreed on in the Snackateria. That design is a team convention. It is not built into the {{profile.vector}} code yet.

### How to read a command

p: Every command has three parts: who you ask, the method with its params, and the text.

- `#data memory:10 water flows` is the ask form. Another entity uses it to ask {{profile.vector}}. The first word names the Deva, the second word holds the method and its params joined by colons, and everything after that is the text.
- `/memory:10 water flows` is the local form. It runs the same method from inside {{profile.vector}} itself. The first word holds the method and its params, and everything after that is the text.

p: The params are numbered from the method. In `#data memory:10 water flows` the method is `memory`, param 1 is `10`, and the text is `water flows`. Each lesson names which param does what for that method.

p: Words in square brackets, such as `[key]` or `[id]`, are placeholders. Replace the whole thing, brackets included, with your own value.

### Lessons

