::BEGIN:MEMORY
# {{prompt.emoji}} Memory
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:memory
	p: Memory is where each entity keeps its own question and answer pairs. Memory lives in the personal database, so every entity has its own database and uses one collection inside it, named `memory`.

	### Searching memory
	- `#data memory:[limit] [words]` searches your `memory` collection for the words.
	- `#data memory:3 wind breath` finds up to 3 entries that match "wind breath".
	- `#data memory [words]` searches with the limit that is already set.

	p: Param 1 is the limit. The default limit is 5. The text is required. With no text, {{profile.vector}} answers with the standard no-text message and does not search.

	p: The search is a Mongo text search over the `q` and `a` fields. Before each search {{profile.vector}} makes sure the text index `a_q_text` exists on the `memory` collection, so it is ready the first time you search it.

	### What a memory result looks like
	p: Each match comes back as a memory container with these lines:
	question: the stored question
	answer: the stored answer
	date: the long date of the created time
	score: the text-search score, with 3 decimals

	p: The results are rendered through Feecting Deva with `feecting parse`, so Feecting Deva must be loaded for /memory to answer. When nothing matches, the text is `no memory`. The raw results are also returned in the answer data, as `data.memory`.

	### How memory is saved
	p: Memory is saved through the `data:memory` event. When an entity talks `data:memory` with a packet, {{profile.vector}} stores one record in the personal database with these fields:
	id: the packet id, which carries the uid
	client: the client id
	agent: the agent id
	q: the question text, cleaned up
	a: the answer text, cleaned up
	created: the time saved, as an epoch number in milliseconds
	md5: the stamp hash of the record
	sha256: the stamp hash of the record
	sha512: the stamp hash of the record

	p: The clean-up joins lines into one line, removes a few stock closing phrases such as "feel free to ask", and squeezes extra spaces.

	### The memory limit stays set
	p: A good limit given with param 1 is saved in the {{profile.vector}} vars and used for later memory searches until someone gives another limit. A bad limit resets it to the default of 5. Saves through `data:memory` always go into the `memory` collection. See the Limits lesson.
::end:memory

