::END:MEMORY

::BEGIN:KNOWLEDGE
# {{prompt.emoji}} Knowledge
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:knowledge
	p: Knowledge is the shared knowledge base. It lives in the global database, in the collection `knowledge`. There are two methods: `know` writes knowledge, and `knowledge` searches it.

	### Writing knowledge with know
	- `#data know [content]` adds a new knowledge record and answers with `id: [id]`.
	- `#data know:[id] [content]` updates the record with that id, and answers with the same `id: [id]`.
	- `#data know water flows to the sea` adds the content "water flows to the sea".

	p: The id is the 24 character Mongo id that the first `know` answered with. The text is required. With no text, {{profile.vector}} answers with the standard no-text message and saves nothing.

	p: A new record stores exactly these fields, plus the `_id` that Mongo adds:
	id: the packet id of the know request, which carries the uid
	content: the text you gave
	created: the time saved, as an epoch number in milliseconds
	modified: null

	p: An update sets `id`, `content` and `modified` on the existing record. The new `modified` is the update time as an epoch number, and `created` stays as it was. The old content is replaced, so an update does not keep the earlier version.

	p: Know stores only these fields. It does not store a writer, a supersedes link or approval votes. Those belong to the team knowledge-card convention, which is not built yet. See the Knowledge Cards lesson.

	### Searching knowledge
	- `#data knowledge:[limit] [words]` searches the content of the knowledge records.
	- `#data knowledge:3 water sea` finds up to 3 records whose content matches "water sea".
	- `#data knowledge [words]` searches with the limit that is already set.

	p: Param 1 is the limit. The default limit is 5. The collection is always `knowledge`, and there is no collection param. The text is required.

	p: The search is a Mongo text search over the `content` field. Before each search {{profile.vector}} makes sure the text index `knowledge_text` exists on `content`.

	### What a knowledge result looks like
	p: Each match comes back as a knowledge container, named with the record `_id`. Inside it is a paragraph line with the content of the record, then these lines:
	created: a long date
	score: the text-search score, with 3 decimals

	p: The results are rendered through Feecting Deva with `feecting parse`, so Feecting Deva must be loaded for /knowledge to answer. When nothing matches, the text is "⛔️ No knowledge found." The raw results are also returned in the answer data, as `data.wisdom`.

	p: Note: the knowledge search only reads back `_id`, `content` and the score. Because `created` is not read back, the created line in a result shows the time of the search, not the time the record was saved.
::end:knowledge

