::END:KNOWLEDGE

::BEGIN:SEARCH
# {{prompt.emoji}} Search
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:search
	p: Search is a general text search over any collection in the global database.

	- `#data search:[collection]:[limit] [words]` searches that collection for the words.
	- `#data search:history:10 water` finds up to 10 records in `history` that match "water".
	- `#data search [words]` searches with the collection and limit that are already set.

	p: Param 1 is the collection. The default collection is `history`. Param 2 is the limit. The default limit is 5. The text is required. With no text, {{profile.vector}} answers with the standard no-text message and does not search.

	p: The search is a Mongo text search. Unlike memory and knowledge, search does not create a text index, so the collection you search must already have one. Use the Indexes lesson to check.

	p: The text answer is `see data`. The results are in the answer data. For each match, search reads back only the answer `a.id`, the answer `a.text` and the score, and it does not return the record `_id`.

	p: The collection and limit you choose stay set for every later search, by any entity, until someone changes them. Always give both params.

	p: Note: the `data:history` event saves history into the personal database, but search reads the global database. When those are two different databases, the default search does not see the saved history. The collection it searches also needs a text index.
::end:search

