::BEGIN:INDEXES
# {{prompt.emoji}} Indexes
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:indexes
	p: The listidx method lists the indexes on a collection in the personal database.

	- `#data listidx:[collection]` lists the indexes with the collection as param 1.
	- `#data listidx [collection]` does the same with the collection as the text.
	- `#data listidx:memory` lists the indexes on the `memory` collection.

	p: The text answer is `indexes`, and the index list is in the answer data. Use it to check that a text index exists before you search a collection.

	p: The text index names that {{profile.vector}} uses are:
	memory: a_q_text, on the q and a fields
	knowledge: knowledge_text, on the content field

	p: Note: listidx reads the personal database, and knowledge lives in the global database. When those are two different databases, listidx does not show the knowledge indexes.
::end:indexes

