::BEGIN:INSERT
# {{prompt.emoji}} Insert
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:insert
	p: Insert writes one document, which you pass as the data of the question, into any collection.

	- `#data insert:[collection]:[database] [text]` inserts the question data into that collection.
	- `/insert:review_docs hello` inserts the data into `review_docs` in the global database.

	p: Param 1 is the collection. Param 2 is the database, and the default is the global database. The document is the data you pass with the question, not the text. The document must carry an `id` with a `uid`, because {{profile.vector}} logs the insert under that uid. Without it the insert fails.

	p: The answer is `id:[id]` with the new Mongo id, and the full insert result is in the answer data.
::end:insert

