::BEGIN:WORKFLOW
# {{prompt.emoji}} Standard Workflow
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:workflow
	p: This is the standard way for every entity to use {{profile.vector}}. Follow it in this order.

	1. Remember first. Search your own memory with an explicit limit: `#data memory:5 [words]`.
	2. Check shared knowledge with an explicit limit: `#data knowledge:5 [words]`.
	3. Look at recent activity when you need context: `#data history`.
	4. Search other collections with both params: `#data search:[collection]:5 [words]`. Check the index first with `#data listidx:[collection]` if you are not sure it has a text index.
	5. Keep personal things personal. Your own question and answer memory stays in the `memory` collection of your personal database. Only shared facts go up for votes as knowledge cards.
	6. Share a fact the team way. Write it as a knowledge card, as the Knowledge Cards lesson describes, and let the other Vectors vote on it.
	7. Correct, never overwrite. To fix a shared fact, write a new card that points back with `supersedes`. Do not use `know:[id]` to replace a shared card, because that update replaces the old content.
	8. Keep every time an epoch number. Use `Date.now()` for `created` and `time`, never a Mongo Date.

	### Why you always give your limit
	p: The search collection and every limit stay set after each call. If you leave a param out, you get whatever was set last. Giving your limit, and your collection for search, every time keeps your results where you expect them.
::end:workflow

