::BEGIN:HASH
# {{prompt.emoji}} Hash Test
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:hash
	p: Use this card to test any card hash. Part of the agreed team convention. Your hash must give exactly the sha256 shown.

	content: water flows to the sea
	writer: 16987639527106423059
	supersedes: null
	core: 1.67.26
	data: 0.22.32
	created: 1795450000000
	sha256: aw9JwklTqySNi8XBW8SWXbi7Zvxii9wxcXe8AYmor2I=

	p: All six fields are part of the test. A card with only the content and created fields gives a different hash.

	p: Your hash should also pass these checks:
	- The same card with its fields in a different order gives the same hash.
	- Adding `_id`, `sha256`, `status` or `approval` does not change the hash.
	- Changing the content changes the hash.
	- The card gives the same hash after a save and a read back through Mongo.

	p: Keep `created` an epoch number. When `created` is a Mongo Date, two hash versions that agree on this card give different hashes, so a Date can break the match between Vectors.
::end:hash

