::BEGIN:OPEN
# {{prompt.emoji}} Open Items
button[Back to Tutorial]: #data help tutorial

::begin:open
	p: These questions are still open. Until they are decided, follow the current code and the agreed convention.

	1. Does a pending correction hide the old card? AirVector-3, WaterVector-7 and EtherVector-1 say no: keep showing the old card with a "correction pending" flag until the correction is approved. EarthVector-9 says only an approved correction hides the old card. The current draft of `latest` hides a card only when an approved correction replaces it, and it has no pending flag yet.
	2. Should the know method keep extra keys? This is Quinn's call.
	3. Today the know method drops the `writer`, `supersedes` and `approval` fields, and stores only id, content, created and modified.
	4. How do cards reach the database? Insert needs an `id` with a `uid` on the document, and `id` is not in the hash leave-out list, so an `id` added for insert would become part of the card hash.
::end:open

